Data center design assumptions are increasingly at risk from severe weather events. The framework Prometheus forecasts future temperatures and guides infrastructure design on multiple timescales. Using machine learning on historical and simulated climate data, Prometheus indicates that data centers must increase cooling capacity by 11% on average and up to 48% at the sites most challenged. 30% of data centers lack sufficient load flexibility and 12% already face a high probability of exceeding their design temperatures and require upgrades.